-- page-pairs this round covers: /articles (list) + /articles/[slug]
-- (detail) — articlesCms's port of articles.php/article.php — and
-- /pharmacists — pharmacistsDirectory's port of the LIVE
-- includes/pharmacy/pharmacists.php tab partial. Applied AFTER
-- 30-/40-/60-phase2-*.sql.tmpl and 70-phase4-batch1-inbox-fixture.sql.tmpl
-- (already piped into the SAME app/tenant DB by parity.mjs's
-- seedDatabase()) — additive only, same pattern every earlier fixture in
-- this directory already established. Does not touch any table an earlier
-- batch already seeds rows into: this file only INSERTs into
-- health_article_categories, health_articles, pharmacists,
-- pharmacist_schedules, pharmacist_holidays, and appointments (`appointments`
-- has no rows from any earlier fixture — grepped every other
-- infra/e2e/seed/*.sql.tmpl file this harness's own FIXTURE_FILES list
-- applies; 55-phase3-batch2-miniapp-fixture.sql.tmpl also inserts into
-- `pharmacists`/`appointments`, but that file belongs to the SEPARATE
-- api-parity.mjs harness — a different docker-compose project, a different
-- freshly-created tenant DB — so there is no id collision risk despite the
-- shared table names).
--
-- No USE statement of its own — same convention as every fixture before it:
-- the caller (parity.mjs's seedDatabase()) prepends `USE \`<app-db>\`;`.
--
-- DETERMINISM: every timestamp is a MySQL relative-date expression
-- (NOW()/CURDATE() +/- INTERVAL n DAY), never a wall-clock literal — same
-- reasoning as every earlier fixture's own header comment. Within ONE
-- multi-row INSERT statement MySQL evaluates NOW()/CURDATE() exactly once
-- and reuses that same instant for every row, so the relative offsets below
-- are self-consistent regardless of how long the statement itself takes to
-- execute, and stay correct forever (time only moves forward) no matter how
-- long after this file is written the harness actually runs.
--
-- ID RANGES: 7501-7503 (health_article_categories), 7601-7605
-- (health_articles), 7701-7703 (pharmacists), 7711-7713
-- (pharmacist_schedules), 7721 (pharmacist_holidays), 7731-7735
-- (appointments) — a batch-specific range that does not overlap any id an
-- earlier infra/e2e/seed/*.sql.tmpl file already uses in these same tables
-- (none do, per the note above) or reuses in tables this file also touches
-- (`users` — this file references EXISTING batch-1 user id 1 for every
-- `appointments.user_id` below, it does not insert any new `users` row).
--
-- WHY NO `line_accounts` ROWS (same invariant every Phase 2 batch since
-- batch 2 has established and reasoned through in full — see
-- 40-phase2-batch2-fixture.sql.tmpl's own header comment for the complete
-- mechanical trace): neither surface this file seeds data for needs one.
--   - articles.php / article.php (and their Next port's queries.ts) resolve
--     `$lineAccountId` via `resolveDefaultLineAccountId()` — SELECT
--     `line_accounts` `is_default=1` else `ORDER BY id ASC LIMIT 1`, and
--     BOTH stacks fall back to the literal `1` when no row is found at all
--     (PHP: `$lineAccount['id'] ?? 1`; Next: `row?.id ?? 1` — read both
--     sources, confirmed identical fallback). Every `health_articles` row
--     below sets `line_account_id = NULL` (not `= 1`) specifically so the
--     query's own `(a.line_account_id = ? OR a.line_account_id IS NULL)`
--     clause matches it regardless of which literal id either stack's
--     fallback actually resolves to — this fixture does not depend on that
--     fallback value at all, by construction.
--   - includes/pharmacy/pharmacists.php's own "Get pharmacists" query (and
--     its Next port, queries.ts::getPharmacistsData()) has NO
--     line_account_id filter whatsoever — grepped the full PHP source and
--     the full port, zero references — so this page has no
--     $currentBotId-hazard to reason about at all, same conclusion batch
--     3's own fixture reached for templates.php.
-- Net: this file, like every fixture since batch 2, seeds ZERO
-- `line_accounts` rows — safe to append onto the SAME shared `phpSid`
-- session every earlier batch's entries already run under, per the
-- acceptance criterion "all NN existing entries still pass, not just the
-- new ones."
--
